    "window_aggregation_rule": "For reading-level personalized detectors evaluated on 60s windows, a window is classified as anomalous (1) if >= 50% of the 1 Hz readings within that window are flagged as overall anomalies (majority vote). The continuous score is the maximum absolute z-score across all physiological channels observed during that window.",
    "alert_latency_policy": "Alert latency is measured as elapsed seconds from genuine stress onset (t=0) to the earliest timestamp of a flagged anomaly (1 Hz) or positive window (60s). If a detector fails to trigger any alert during the entire stress condition (missed detection), the latency is right-censored at the total duration of the stress evaluation period.",
